            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "The new link removal (RetireDroppedPiAgentLinks in engine/runtime/pi_agents.go) acts only on symlinks that read back as exactly the package's own agents/\u003cfile\u003e path. That check is the same ownership proof that Uninstall already relies on. Foreign files, gentle-pi links, links into other packages and non-.md links are left alone, and the tests in engine/runtime/pi_agents_test.go and engine/cmd/pipkg_test.go cover each of these cases.",
              "The one new reach into the home directory is `pipkg build` retiring links under ~/.pi/agent/agents. It is limited to links that point into the --dest-dir package, and `pipkg check` changes nothing (covered by TestRunPipkgCore_CheckRetiresNothing). I found no path traversal, secret exposure or injection route in the change.",
              "Removing the fallback to the generic agents/GADU.md and deleting pi/agents/GADU.md are intended behaviour changes with no security impact. The unreadable-package-agents case is guarded: nothing is retired if the package's agents directory cannot be listed. No dependency or lockfile changes are in the candidate."
            ]
          }
        }
