            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 26 changed paths for resilience. Link retirement runs right after the package build in the pipkg build verb and in the adapter's Install, Update and Rollback, so it happens even when pi is absent from PATH or `pi install` fails. A stale GADU.md link therefore cannot outlive the file it pointed at.",
              "Ownership is proven by readlink equality with the package's own agents/\u003cfile\u003e. Foreign files, gentle-pi links and links into other packages are never removed, and the new tests cover each of these cases.",
              "Failure handling degrades safely. An empty home, an unreadable package agents directory or a failed removal retires nothing or reports a note, and the build or install result does not fail. The read-only `pipkg check` removes nothing. Status now reports an overlay-owned link that no package agent backs as stale, and reports an unlistable links directory as unproven.",
              "The new directory listing is a single ReadDir per build, so it adds no meaningful latency or load, and I found no retry-safety problem. Re-running the build is idempotent: a second run finds no owned stale link and prints no extra output.",
              "Removing the GADU.md fallback in copyPiAgents is a requested change. It gives an overlay with no pi/agents a package with no agents, and the tests cover this."
            ]
          }
        }
