            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R3-pipkg-build-uses-home-env",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/cmd/pipkg.go:92-94",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "pipkg build now retires links under the home from runtimeConfigFromEnv, a side effect outside --dest-dir. Only symlinks that read back as the package's own agents/\u003cfile\u003e are removed, so the blast radius is small. The home comes from the environment, though, not from a flag. A build run with a different HOME, such as a CI sandbox, silently looks at another home. This is covered by tests for the HOME-set and HOME-empty cases, but nothing proves that an explicit dest-dir outside the state dir leaves a real home alone.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/cmd/pipkg_test.go:300-322",
                  "engine/runtime/pi_agents.go:312-342"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 26 manifest paths in the patch.",
              "Removing the GADU fallback in copyPiAgents is tested by the pipkg tests: a Pi file is shipped, the Claude file is never shipped, and no pi/agents gives an empty package.",
              "RetireDroppedPiAgentLinks is exercised through the adapter's Install without pi on PATH, Install with a failing pi install, Update and Rollback, the pipkg build command, the shell helper, and Status. The tests cover foreign files, foreign links, non-.md links, unreadable directories and the unreadable-package-agents case. Retirement is skipped when the package agents cannot be listed.",
              "Retirement requires readlink equality with the package's own path, so foreign files and links are left alone. Failures are reported in the message and do not fail the build.",
              "Status now reports a stale owned link and an unlistable agents directory as partial. Golden files are updated consistently.",
              "No blocking reliability regression found."
            ]
          }
        }
      }
